  "goodToKnow": "Brutto means gross, before deductions: das Bruttogehalt, 3.000 Euro brutto. Netto is what's left: in Germany, social insurance and taxes can take 35 to 45 percent of a salary, so the Brutto-Netto-Rechner is a popular online tool. Das Bruttoinlandsprodukt (BIP) is GDP. Prices include VAT, so they're also brutto. From Italian brutto (raw, ugly), via merchants' language."
